board	the board holds 161 tickets, of which 84 are repeat filings of 42 distinct objectives. An append-only record cannot retract a filing, so these are reported rather than removed, and the ticket count above is NOT a count of distinct pieces of work
board-duplicate	86 and 130, 172	add RecordState::Contested for the case where the ACTION is settled and a CONSEQUENCE is owed — because Unresolved says no answer was given and Superseded says a newer one replaced it, and neither is what happened
board-duplicate	97 and 141, 183	add a behavioural census axis whose cell is a NAMED TEST PATH the coverage matrix forces every crate to fill — derived from this record format, not from the old tree's per-part claim gate
board-duplicate	92 and 136, 178	admit the baseline atmosphere as TICK-ZERO DATA with a source per number, instead of four f64 constants in a shaper — because that admission is the exact thing the other tree is blocked without
board-duplicate	69 and 113, 155	build the fixed 20 Hz clock with an accumulator that bounds how many missed ticks one slow frame may catch up on, and count what it dropped
board-duplicate	58 and 102, 144	build the shell-owned notification queue: one writer, one rendering per record, one at a time
board-duplicate	66 and 110, 152	carry every sky constant in a provenance inventory that names its source, and count the project extensions in a test so an unsourced number cannot be added silently
board-duplicate	85 and 129, 171	carry pressure, temperature and flow as fixed-point integers at a DECLARED scale, so a threshold test is an exact integer comparison, and bind the scale into identity so changing it refuses an old save
board-duplicate	89 and 133, 175	declare the voxel-to-metre scale as one constant with a named source, and bind it into identity — because the world states a density in kg/m^3 and holds a lattice in voxels with no declared number between them
board-duplicate	77 and 121, 163	delete the second air column: one function answers what a light ray's path loses, and both the noon normaliser and the sun's own colour read it
board-duplicate	83 and 127, 169	derive soil porosity HERE from a named source, or refuse every porosity this tree states — because the only number available is another tree's provisional row with its own tolerance undefined
board-duplicate	75 and 119, 161	derive the extra subvoxel shapers from the gas and fluid ruling rather than inventing them, so a machine's behaviour is a consequence of what a fluid is and not a list of shapes
board-duplicate	57 and 101, 143	dock a window: hit-test a drag to a pane or an outer edge, preview the zone, and insert on drop
board-duplicate	60 and 104, 146	enforce the unenforced halves of the craft floor in voxel-ui as refusals: depth offset, measure, motion easing, copy naming recovery
board-duplicate	67 and 111, 153	evaluate sky radiance from the real scattering models so the sky's colour is the model's output: Rayleigh and Mie coefficients, the Henyey-Greenstein phase function, and Kasten-Young air mass
board-duplicate	65 and 109, 151	give SkyPhase the real twilight thresholds of -6, -12 and -18 degrees plus golden hour, blue hour and the Belt of Venus, and test each at its exact boundary angle
board-duplicate	90 and 134, 176	give a subvoxel cell a DECLARED EXACT VOLUME, so a cell's mass is volume times bulk density as an exact rational and a cell can hold matter
board-duplicate	79 and 123, 165	give every decision in this record a status and a hazard beside it, and a withdrawal record that supersedes a wrong claim by id — so a settled decision carries what could still break it
board-duplicate	68 and 112, 154	give the night a source that is not the sun dimmed: the Moon's real phase derived from tick at the published Bond albedo, so a night is not the day with a smaller number
board-duplicate	81 and 125, 167	key the surface displacement by (structure, material, face) instead of (material, face) for the whole world, so two machines may pattern the same wall without one refusing the other
board-duplicate	62 and 106, 148	make Openness::Settled constructible, so a reader of the record can see that a question is answered
board-duplicate	64 and 108, 150	make solar position a pure function of (tick, declared latitude): declination and hour angle to altitude and azimuth, with no clock and no RNG
board-duplicate	78 and 122, 164	make the moon a REFLECTANCE on a lit surface — solar constant at its orbit, Bond albedo as a SourcedReflectance, attenuated back through the same air column — instead of an independent emitter
board-duplicate	72 and 116, 158	measure the sky offscreen: read the pixels back and show that the clear colour and the rig both change with the tick, so 'the sky is lit' is a number rather than a claim
board-duplicate	95 and 139, 181	prove every gate reading can go RED — a mutation check on the values the gate measures, because a suite that cannot go red is not evidence and a number asserted in isolation can be a number that goes nowhere
board-duplicate	61 and 105, 147	re-audit each feature row's means text against what its witness actually contains, and stop reporting active when the witness is thinner than the feature
