board-duplicate	82 and 126, 168	rule that air is SEVERAL NAMED POOLS mixing only through declared processes, with a stored global account and per-basin accounts cross-checked at audit — not one global scalar and not one account
board-duplicate	93 and 137, 179	rule that climate is NOT a regional field — temperature, moisture, precipitation, humidity, pressure, wind and storms are PROCESSES — and that the field ladder therefore carries lithology, elevation and soil depth only
board-duplicate	87 and 131, 173	rule that withdrawing a decision does NOT refute what it described, and carry a flag saying so — or a later reader will 'fix' a seam that was left open on purpose
